  "articles": [
    {
      "title": "MemBrain",
      "url": "https://bindingofisaacrebirth.wiki.gg/wiki/MemBrain",
      "revision_url": "https://bindingofisaacrebirth.wiki.gg/index.php?oldid=267035",
      "revision": 267035,
      "timestamp": "2026-07-29T16:10:53Z",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "attribution": "The Binding of Isaac: Rebirth Wiki contributors",
      "sections": [
        {
          "heading": "Introduction",
          "level": 0,
          "text": "MemBrains are much larger Brains that slowly move around the room and occasionally hop to fire 8 blood shots in all directions. They have a large amount of health and will split into two Brains upon death. Membrains deal a whole heart of damage with contact and projectiles."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Variants",
          "level": 2,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "heading": "Mama Guts",
          "level": 3,
          "text": "Mama Guts are large versions of the regular Guts. They slowly move around the room, occasionally hopping and firing 8 large blood shots in all directions. Upon death, it splits into 2 Guts."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Dead Meat",
          "level": 3,
          "text": "Dead Meats are bigger versions of the Cysts that move around the room slowly, occasionally hopping which fires 8 large blood shots in all directions that bounce off the walls like Rubber Cement. Upon death, they split into 2 Cysts."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Dinga",
          "level": 3,
          "text": "Dingas are large Dips that behave similarly to MemBrains. Dingas slide around the room aimlessly and occasionally hop, spawning Dips or shooting poop shots in 8 directions. Splits into two Squirts when killed."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Mega Clotty",
          "level": 3,
          "text": "Mega Clotties slowly move around the room, occasionally hopping. When one hops, it will usually fire six blood shots around itself, but it can also alternatively leave a puddle of Red Creep near itself. Even more rarely, the hop may spawn a Clotty or a collapsed Globin. Upon death, it\u2019ll split into two Clotty. Even though the sprite shows three conjoined Clotties, it always creates two upon death, and will never spawn three."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Gallery",
          "level": 2,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "heading": "Notes",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "\u2022 All monsters listed on this page deal one whole heart of contact damage except for Mega Clotty which deals half a heart of contact damage."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Trivia",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "\u2022 MemBrain is a pun on the word membrane, which means a thin, flexible layer of body tissue.\n\n\u2022 Mama Guts slightly resembles a digestive system.\n\n\u2022 [Afterbirth onward] The Mega Clotty\u2019s behavior coincidentally bears some resemblance to a fan idea of a boss called \u201cMega Clotty,\u201d as, besides its name, this 2012 idea mentions that its behavior would be jumping up to shoot out blood shots as well as spawning one Clotty. However, the Mega Clotty is implemented as an enemy, not a boss, and some of its conceptual behaviors on the ideas wiki were never implemented for the fact that it\u2019s purely coincidental. [end edition note]"
        }
      ],
